      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Grok4F Snark has Daretti, Scrap Savant available to cast for 4 mana (3R) and has exactly the mana to do so (Mountain, Phyrexia's Core for colorless, Plains x2, plus Mycosynth Wellspring is an artifact not a land). Looking at the board: Mountain provides R, Plains x2 provide WW, Phyrexia's Core provides C, and Archaeomancer's Map is an artifact. So available mana is R, W, W, C = 4 mana with only 1 red. Daretti costs {3}{R} which is exactly payable. Daretti would provide card filtering (+2 to discard up to 2 and draw that many), which is very valuable with expensive cards like Myr Battlesphere and Combustible Gearhulk in hand. Pilgrim's Eye costs {3} and fetches a basic land - useful but slower. However, playing Daretti first allows immediate +2 loyalty (going to 5), letting Snark discard expensive cards like Myr Battlesphere to draw fresh cards, and sets up the -2 artifact reanimation ability for future turns. Pilgrim's Eye is fine value but Daretti on turn 4 with artifacts already in play (Mycosynth Wellspring to potentially sacrifice) is likely stronger. That said, Pilgrim's Eye does fix mana and provide a body, and Daretti might be vulnerable on a multiplayer board. This is close but Daretti seems better here.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Pilgrim's Eye for 3 mana to search for a basic land",
      "better_line": "Cast Daretti, Scrap Savant for {3}{R}, immediately +2 to discard expensive cards (Myr Battlesphere, Combustible Gearhulk) and draw replacements, setting up future -2 reanimation with Mycosynth Wellspring or other artifacts",
