      "description": "Gem3P Romance cast Dragonspeaker Shaman (a 2/2 creature with no immediate impact) before casting Lightning Greaves. The Shaman has no haste and is vulnerable to removal for an entire turn cycle. Lightning Greaves costs only 2 mana with 0 equip cost, and could have been cast first to protect the Shaman immediately after casting it. However, with only 5 lands available (and some entering tapped), the sequencing matters: Dragonspeaker Shaman costs 1RR and Lightning Greaves costs 2. With Savage Lands (B/R/G), Vivid Crag (R or any with counter), Seaside Citadel (G/W/U), and Vivid Meadow (tapped), they likely had exactly 3 mana available after Vivid Meadow was tapped. They could cast the Shaman for 1RR using Savage Lands (R) + Vivid Crag (R) + one other land for colorless... but Seaside Citadel produces G/W/U, not colorless for Greaves. So they had exactly 3 colored mana that could cast the Shaman but likely couldn't cast both in one turn. Still, casting Lightning Greaves first would have been better - it's a permanent that protects future creatures, and the Shaman without protection is fragile. Playing Greaves this turn and Shaman next turn (immediately equipping for free) would protect the key cost-reducer.",
