      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Discarding Reconstruct History means losing the ability to recover multiple card types from the graveyard later. Reconstruct History could return an artifact, enchantment, instant, sorcery, and planeswalker from the graveyard — it's a powerful recursion spell that gets better as the game goes on, especially in an Osgir artifact-heavy deck where cards will naturally end up in the graveyard. Meanwhile, Myr Battlesphere at 7 mana is extremely expensive and may never be castable efficiently (Osgir can potentially copy it from the graveyard anyway via exile ability), and Combustible Gearhulk at 6 mana is also very expensive. Discarding one of those high-cost creatures would be better since Osgir can potentially reconstruct them from the graveyard, and Reconstruct History itself could later retrieve discarded artifacts.",
