    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "With 8 mana available (3 Plains, 1 Mountain, 1 Phyrexia's Core, plus Archaeomancer's Map doesn't tap for mana), Grok4F Snark has access to about 5-6 mana. Losheel, Clockwork Scholar (2W) would provide card draw whenever artifact creatures enter and prevent combat damage to attacking artifact creatures - synergizing well with the Pilgrim's Eye already on board and the Combustible Gearhulk in hand. Quicksmith Genius (2R) only triggers on artifact ETB with a loot effect. Losheel provides pure card advantage (draw without discard) and defensive utility, while Quicksmith Genius only loots. However, Quicksmith Genius at 3 mana leaves mana open for other plays, and the loot effect could help find lands or dump artifacts for Osgir in the graveyard. The decision is debatable but Losheel seems stronger in this board state, especially since next turn casting Combustible Gearhulk with Losheel out would draw a card.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Quicksmith Genius (2R) instead of Losheel, Clockwork Scholar",
      "better_line": "Cast Losheel, Clockwork Scholar (2W) to get card draw from future artifact creature ETBs (including Combustible Gearhulk next turn) and protect attacking artifact creatures from combat damage",
      "type": "blunder",
