      "player": "Grok4F Snark",
      "decision_index": 148,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Casting Losheel, Clockwork Scholar (2W) before combat means the opponent knows about the damage prevention for attacking artifact creatures before blocks are declared. Additionally, casting Combustible Gearhulk (4RR) might not be castable this turn with the available mana (Mountain + 3 Plains + Phyrexia's Core + Archaeomancer's Map = only 1 red source), so Losheel is a reasonable play. However, with Daretti, Scrap Savant available as an alternative, Daretti could be cast (3R) using Mountain + 3 other lands, allowing the +2 to discard and draw, potentially improving hand quality and setting up graveyard recursion for the Myr Battlesphere or Rout in the graveyard. Daretti's -2 could sacrifice Mycosynth Wellspring (getting a land search) and return Myr Battlesphere from the graveyard, which would be a very powerful play. With 5 mana available (Mountain, 3 Plains, Phyrexia's Core), casting Daretti for 3R is possible (Mountain for R, 3 other lands for generic), then using -2 to sacrifice Mycosynth Wellspring and return Myr Battlesphere would be a massive tempo swing.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Losheel, Clockwork Scholar for 2W",
