    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "During combat (likely an opponent's turn given the context), GPT5m chose to flash in Nymris, Oona's Trickster instead of Hullbreaker Horror. Nymris is a 1/6 flyer that provides card advantage when casting spells on opponents' turns, while Hullbreaker Horror is a 7/8 uncounterable threat that bounces spells/permanents whenever you cast a spell. Hullbreaker Horror is generally a much more impactful card and harder to deal with. However, GPT5m has 8 mana sources (6 lands + Dimir Signet + Island), so they have exactly 7 mana for Hullbreaker Horror (5UU). Nymris costs 3UB (5 mana), which is cheaper and leaves mana open. The key consideration is that Nymris enables the card-draw trigger immediately on subsequent opponent turns, while Hullbreaker Horror needs follow-up spells to generate value. With only a few cards in hand after casting either, Hullbreaker might not have immediate fuel. Still, Hullbreaker Horror's raw power level and the fact that it can't be countered make it generally the stronger play when you can cast it, especially as a defensive measure. This is debatable depending on the game plan.",
