    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "With only one opponent remaining (Grok4F Snark at 24hp) and Hullbreaker Horror in hand, the key question is whether to deploy Nightveil Sprite now or hold up mana for Arcane Denial and save resources. Nightveil Sprite is a 1/2 flyer that provides surveil, which is decent but modest. The main concern is that casting a creature before combat is generally suboptimal when holding combat tricks, but more importantly, casting Nightveil Sprite uses 2 mana, leaving 7 lands + Dimir Signet available (so 8 mana sources minus 2 = 6 remaining). This still leaves enough to hold up Arcane Denial (2 mana). However, Blightwing Bandit (3B) would be a stronger play since it has flying, deathtouch, and its ability to exile cards from opponents' libraries when casting spells on their turns synergizes well with the reactive gameplan (holding up Arcane Denial). With 8 mana available, casting Blightwing Bandit (4 mana) still leaves 4 mana for Arcane Denial. Blightwing Bandit is strictly better here as a threat - 2/2 flying deathtouch vs 1/2 flying surveil, and the exile ability generates card advantage.",
